    <!-- Icon grid contract

         Every icon is drawn on a 24x24 grid, centred on (12,12), and authored so its
         LONGEST side measures exactly 20 units.

         That rule is what makes the set line up. These are rendered with Stretch="Uniform"
         into a square box, and Uniform scales by min(box/width, box/height) — so if one icon's
         ink is 18 wide and another's is 15, they get different scale factors, different stroke
         weights, and different optical left edges. Pinning the longest side to 20 forces the
         same divisor for every icon, and Uniform then centres each one identically.

         Consequence: an icon that is naturally narrow (the bolt) stays narrow. That is correct
         — it should look narrow, it just must not be scaled up to compensate.

         Call sites must use a SQUARE box (Width == Height) or the rule does not hold.

         The two caption glyphs at the bottom are deliberately outside this set: they live
         alone in the title bar and are sized to the Windows convention, not to this grid.
    -->

